==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 60~73.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Bore]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 333.33 seconds<sup>10,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Nimoy Bore]]s spawn after 313.33 seconds<sup>9,400f</sup>, delay 333.33 seconds<sup>10,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mooth]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Manic Flying Cat (Enemy)|Manic Flying Cat]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
The Manic Flying Cat can be hard to push back due to its extreme range, high damage and having only 1 knockback, so you'll have to use tankers or bulky units like Jamiera Cat, rather than backliners like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]]. The [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] and [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] items also help. [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], especially with freeze effect up talent, can be an effective counter to Nimoy Bore.

[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] can be an effective counter to stop the Bore. Stacking [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is amazing in this level since the fast pushers will be slowed. Similarly, [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]], if you have him, is a great team with Cyberpunk Cat and can pin most of the enemies to the base. [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly/Fishman Cat]] is very helpful for chipping down Manic Flying Cat (and also helps with the Mooth), and so is [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako/Octopus]] can be used to tank and stall Manic Flying Cat in place, not to mention his chance to weaken Manic Flying Cat as well. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] can also be used to tank when the boss is alone. It is usually recommended to use Awakened Bahamut Cat to kill the Rain D.s rather than chip down the Bores or Manic Flying Cat, as he will only get at most two hits on the boss, while the Bores could potentially reach and cycle him quickly.

Because of the lack of money supply in this stage, using minimal meatshields can be a viable way to beat the stage, as you get more money to spend on damage dealers. Although keep in mind, not using meatshields will cause you to slowly lose ground over time, meaning you are fighting against the clock to kill the boss.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] - Resistant to Floating as well as having a chance to weaken them to 50%, Sadako is perfect for stalling the boss when there are no peons on the field. However, they die very quickly to the Rain Ds present in the stage, so you are going to need to protect them well. Unless you have Octopus's [[Talents]], use Sadako Cat for their faster attack rate.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera]] - The two titan variants work very well on this stage, as their high health pool allows for them survive a hit or two from Manic Flying, which makes a huge difference in mitigating its pushing power.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A simple solution to the Bores in the stage, a level 40 Courier also has enough damage output to juggle the Rain Ds when timed properly. However, they die instantly to the Manic Flying, so be careful when using them.
*[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] - A no-brainer if you want to stall the Bore without losing too much ground: iCat is very powerful at crowd controlling Bore without it pushing too much. However their range is extremely low, so don't rely on them surviving for too long.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - An answer to the Nimoy Bore present in the stage, but with his raw HP and guaranteed survive ability, he can land a hit or two on the boss before dying.
*[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale]] - If used together, synergizes very well with iCat as they can melt down the Bore and provide additional chip damage against the boss. If you have a bonus slot in your lineup, you can fit a [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fisherman Cat]] in your lineup for a unit defense up [[Moby Dick (Combo)|combo]] that works extremely well with the titan variants.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that has a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] or [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies should do well here, as long as they are good enough to fulfill their roles in battle, that be [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controlling]] the Bores, [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|nuking]] Manic Flying Cat, or anything else of the sort. Below are more specified examples of good [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] to use in this stage.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]]: His extremely long-range makes it so he can outrange even Manic Flying Cat, as well as being able to keep Manic Flying Cat at bay due to his [[Knockback|knockback]] (and [[Freeze|freeze]] if you managed to get his [[True Form]]) ability. Ultimately, if there are at least two of them, they will be able to run towards the base when another Cosmo is knocking the boss back, possibly winning you the fight while Manic Flying is still alive.
*[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]]: Her rapid [[Long Distance]] attacks combined with her [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies speeds this stage up a lot.
*[[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|Strike Unit R.E.I.]]: Same as Saber minus the Long Distance and rapid attacks (unless you have R.E.I.'s True Form).
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]]: Same as R.E.I, but tankier, stronger (Even against non-floating) and more spammable, although she attacks and moves slower (Works better with True Form).
*[[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka]]: A [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] with [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies and can rebound easily after getting hit by anything, just make sure to only use him on Manic Flying Cat and/or Nimoy Bore.
*[[Heracrist (Uber Rare Cat)|Heracrist]]: In their Normal Form, they can be used against Manic Flying Cat. In their Evolved Form, they can be used against Nimoy Bore. The Normal Form is more recommended for this battle specifically though, due to their insane attack power that allows them to kill Manic Flying Cat quickly.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Lesser Demon Cat]]: Basically the same as Heracrist, but its True Form is recommended for the highest success rate. Does great damage at close range, which combined with the low cost and fast recharge allows it to be easily replaced whenever it's destroyed.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: With its True Form, Lufalan Pasalan outranges even the boss (720 vs 640) and as there are only powerful individual enemies here with high health, it can work well. Its 20% critical chance can also drastically speed up the fight by dealing a whopping 200K damage per hit, while also heavily damaging the Bore variants, one shotting Mooth, and crippling the Rain Ds.

